<BaseLayout title="Theses" description="Investment theses from The Vin Diagram.">
  <article class="prose" style="padding: 2rem 0 4rem;">
    <h1>Theses</h1>
    <p>I have a few core theses about the world that shape my philosophy as an early-stage investor. They help guide <strong>why</strong> I invest along with <strong>what</strong> and <strong>who</strong> I invest in.</p>
    <p><strong>Why:</strong> I believe technology and capital are powerful tools for social progress. The remarkable rise in human living standards over the past 200 years is directly attributable to these forces.</p>
    <p><strong>What:</strong> The last two decades of innovation have been driven largely by the paradigmatic shift in computing infrastructure to the cloud. I believe the next two decades of innovation will be driven by a shift towards AI-enabled software and services.</p>
    <p><strong>Who:</strong> I believe talent is universal, opportunity is not. I aim to work with the &ldquo;outsiders&rdquo; and I am constantly inspired by the incredible things daring founders can accomplish when all odds are against them.</p>
  </article>
